[h1]Weapon Borders[/h1]
Ever wonder which starting weapons you've actually beaten each danger with? Characters get a colored border for the highest danger you've won with them. [b]Now your starting weapons do too.[/b]

On the weapon selection screen, each weapon is colored by the [b]highest danger you've beaten while starting with it[/b], using the same colors as the character borders.

[h2]How it works[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Per zone[/b] - progress is tracked separately for each zone, just like characters.
[*][b]What counts as a win[/b] - surviving wave 20 or killing the final boss. In [b]endless[/b], the win counts as soon as you survive wave 20.
[*][b]Co-op[/b] - every player's starting weapon gets credit.
[*][b]Random zone[/b] - the zone is rolled before the weapon screen, so borders show your progress for the zone you're about to play.
[*][b]Nightmare[/b] - supported, with the same frame as characters.
[/list]

[h2]Good to know[/h2]
[list]
[*]Only tracks runs [b]started with the mod installed[/b] - your past wins aren't recorded per weapon by the base game, so everything starts uncolored.
[*]Purely visual - your weapons and save are untouched. Progress is stored in its own file: [i]%APPDATA%\Brotato\mod_weapon_borders.json[/i]
[*]Built for Brotato 1.2.0.0.
[/list]

